{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Ashrei</b> — The reason for mentioning all this is that in Your hand are strength and might, and kindness and truth surround You. If so, why do You delay to establish Your covenant and the kindness You promised us?!" "And the meaning of <b>ashrei ha-am</b> — after kindness and justice, is that by Your might and Your righteousness You save all who call upon Your name." "And the meaning of <b>teru'ah</b> — like: ותרועת מלך בו." "<b>Be'or paneikha yehalekhun</b> — like: לאורו אלך חשך."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:32.675867389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}